erfly@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="458101" owner_email="andreyu@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/overlays/board-overlays" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/board-overlays" ref="refs/changes/01/458101/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I9ccd34a47f21f6ab6f8c15b9cdce523b1f84022c" commit="412af2298c9aeb8d0e7a5fc13cb578a080d12ccb" commit_message="[autotest] Tweak the error message of the sysrq repair action.  When repairing a DUT by pressing sysrq-x failed, the error message was the same as the error message for reset via servo.  This changes both messages to be clear about which operation failed.  BUG=None TEST=run repair, see the new sysrq-x message  Change-Id: I9ccd34a47f21f6ab6f8c15b9cdce523b1f84022c Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/457831 Commit-Ready: Richard Barnette &lt;jrbarnette@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Richard Barnette &lt;jrbarnette@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Xixuan Wu &lt;xixuan@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="457831" owner_email="jrbarnette@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/31/457831/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I39013ab05e1f072ae790f853c3e2f845bd780185" commit="c37b6f0a7b906624da5bbcffeb17275bd7c89b90" commit_message="mmc: Set a default value for the clock variable  GCC found that the clock variable could be used without being set.  Set it to 1 which is used by mmc_setup_media() below to initialize to the lowest valid frequency before we have read any descriptors.  This and will usually end up as 400KHz after the clamping in mmc_set_clock())  This warning was causing a build failure: src/drivers/storage/mmc.c:503:8: error: 'clock' may be used uninitialized in this function [-Werror=maybe-uninitialized]  BUG=none BRANCH=none TEST=Build now passes in upstream coreboot  Change-Id: I39013ab05e1f072ae790f853c3e2f845bd780185 Signed-off-by: Martin Roth &lt;martinroth@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/457811 Commit-Ready: Martin Roth &lt;martinroth@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Martin Roth &lt;martinroth@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Julius Werner &lt;jwerner@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="457811" owner_email="martinroth@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" ref="refs/changes/11/457811/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I6e5bf843b88c1feb9406fbe2b309087e6d21beab" commit="7a4f29afe047099d9bc193f7f8c09b992844bbb7" commit_message="change Event entities to be consistent with CIDB  &quot;package&quot; -&gt; &quot;name&quot; &quot;end_time&quot; -&gt; &quot;finish_time&quot; &quot;status&quot; = &quot;pass&quot;|&quot;fail&quot;  BUG=chromium:703431 TEST=cros_event_unittest  Change-Id: I6e5bf843b88c1feb9406fbe2b309087e6d21beab Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/459678 Commit-Ready: Chris Ching &lt;chingcodes@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Chris Ching &lt;chingcodes@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: David Riley &lt;davidriley@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="459678" owner_email="chingcodes@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/chromite" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/chromite" ref="refs/changes/78/459678/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ib036e88a84eb5c3b7ac3092d298965bf374ceee8" commit="37fb95617b58ff278c3cd81f949a0970a123e233" commit_message="cheets_CTSHelper: Drop init_network_controller argument.  [*** DO NOT INTEGRATE TO R58 ***] On R59 this became false by default so it is not