s doesn't permit cases where we want a device to be usable but not to produce wakeups (imagine the tablet-mode behavior of a keyboard device that also reports events from a side power button).  Now, if the &quot;wakeup&quot; tag is set and at least one of &quot;wakeup_when_laptop&quot;, &quot;wakeup_when_docked&quot;, &quot;wakeup_when_tablet&quot;, and &quot;wakeup_when_display_off&quot; is set, the device will be configured to only produce wakeups while the system is in one of the requested modes.  Also add a short doc describing how powerd interprets input devices' udev tags.  BUG=chromium:703691 TEST=updated unit tests  Change-Id: I1138782052f0370b8df7f0133b79ed1e8494f21a Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/459439 Commit-Ready: Dan Erat &lt;derat@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Dan Erat &lt;derat@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Eric Caruso &lt;ejcaruso@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="459439" owner_email="derat@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/39/459439/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I7576dd6a19c9a260abd4eb2f43e2238685150a8a" commit="39f2be31601f4a3eca9dffd70e245df47a02cf87" commit_message="Align bitbang spi handling with upstream  half_period is now kept in the master's struct, instead of passed by argument to the init function.  bitbang_spi_init() is renamed to register_spi_bitbang_master().  BUG=chromium:478356 BRANCH=none TEST=still builds  Change-Id: I7576dd6a19c9a260abd4eb2f43e2238685150a8a Signed-off-by: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/458401 Commit-Ready: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Stefan Reinauer &lt;reinauer@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="458401" owner_email="pgeorgi@chromium